WEBVTT

00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:03.804
Africa has a wealth of experience
in dealing with epidemics,

00:03:03.804 --> 00:03:05.056
such as cholera,

00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:06.390
Ebola and measles,

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.391
to name a few.

00:03:07.808 --> 00:03:11.229
Some African countries have strong
contact tracing systems

00:03:11.229 --> 00:03:14.190
as well as very strong
community health networks.

00:03:14.732 --> 00:03:18.986
So we needed to draw on
our strengths and experience,

00:03:18.986 --> 00:03:22.782
prioritizing solutions
which we knew would save African lives.

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:25.826
For example, the provision
of medical oxygen,

00:03:25.826 --> 00:03:29.872
whose shortage I was highlighting
as early as March 2020,

00:03:29.872 --> 00:03:32.875
and which we’re perfectly capable
of producing in Africa,